   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( y = f(x) \\) be the solution to the differential equation \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = y \\left(x + 1\\right) \\) with \\( f(0) = 2 \\). Find the approximation to \\( f(1) \\) given by Euler's method, starting at \\( x = 0 \\) with two steps of equal size. Give the exact value."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         21,
         4
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The step size is \\( \\Delta x = \\frac{1 - (0)}{2} = \\frac{1}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At \\( (0, 2) \\) the slope is \\( 2 \\), so \\( y \\approx 2 + (\\frac{1}{2})(2) = 3 \\) at \\( x = \\frac{1}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( (\\frac{1}{2}, 3) \\) the slope is \\( \\frac{9}{2} \\), so \\( y \\approx 3 + (\\frac{1}{2})(\\frac{9}{2}) = \\frac{21}{4} \\) at \\( x = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            21,
            4
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( f(1) \\approx \\frac{21}{4} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            21,
            4
         ]
      }
